{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<?ui-args --schema urn:example:ext=tests/ui/schemas/extension.xsd?>\n<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" xmlns:x=\"urn:example:ext\" initial=\"a\">\n  <state id=\"a\">\n    <x:note>reviewed</x:note>\n    <transition event=\"go\" target=\"done\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"done\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/limit006-foreign-element.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":1,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":0},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/limit006-foreign-element.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":30,"byteOffset":184,"endColumn":30,"endLine":4,"startColumn":17,"startLine":3},"insertedContent":{"text":""}}]}],"description":{"text":"remove `<x:note>`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/limit006-foreign-element.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":12,"endLine":4,"startColumn":6,"startLine":4}}}],"message":{"markdown":"this compiler cannot lower `<x:note>` from namespace `urn:example:ext` inside `<state>`\n\n**Note:** this is a limit of this toolchain, not an SCXML rule: SCXML 1.0 allows elements from other namespaces in its content models (the W3C schema's `##other` wildcards), but the compiler lowers them only as executable content (custom actions in `<onentry>`, `<onexit>`, `<transition>`, `<finalize>`, `<if>`, or `<foreach>`) and rejects them anywhere else rather than drop them silently\n\n**Help:** to compile the document with this toolchain, move the element into executable content, or remove it","text":"this compiler cannot lower `<x:note>` from namespace `urn:example:ext` inside `<state>`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":196,"start":190},"category":"internal"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"this compiler lowers only SCXML children of `<state>`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/limit006-foreign-element.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":9,"endLine":3,"startColumn":4,"startLine":3}}}],"ruleId":"LIMIT006"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"this is a limit of this toolchain, not an SCXML rule: SCXML 1.0 allows attributes from other namespaces (`xml:lang`, `xsi:schemaLocation`, editor or custom attributes) on its elements and elements from other namespaces in its content models (the W3C schema's `##other` wildcards), but the compiler lowers foreign elements only as executable content (custom actions) and carries no foreign attribute into Machine IR; it rejects the rest rather than drop them silently, so the document cannot compile"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: to compile the document with this toolchain, remove the attribute or element (an `xml:*` or `xsi:*` attribute carries no SCXML behavior), or move extension data into a custom action in executable content.\n\nRun `scx --explain LIMIT006` for examples."},"id":"LIMIT006","name":"LIMIT006","properties":{"category":"internal"},"shortDescription":{"text":"this compiler cannot lower an attribute or element from another namespace here"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}